            </p>
            <div class="flex gap-2 text-xs">
              <a href="/convert/csv-to-json" class="underline font-semibold text-[#111111] dark:text-[#f0f0f2]">csv to json</a>
              <span>•</span>
              <a href="/convert/json-to-csv" class="underline font-semibold text-[#111111] dark:text-[#f0f0f2]">json to csv</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 5: Step-by-Step Guide on How to Compare JSON -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#111111] dark:text-[#f0f0f2]">
          How to Compare JSON Files Online in 4 Easy Steps
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Getting started with our <strong>json compare online</strong> tool takes only seconds. Follow these four quick steps to pinpoint differences:
        </p>
        <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[#4b4b4d] dark:text-[#9ca3af]">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-[#111111] dark:text-[#f0f0f2]">Input Your JSON Payloads:</strong> Paste your baseline (Left) and modified (Right) JSON documents directly into the editors, or click "Load File" to import <code>.json</code> documents from your local drive.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-[#111111] dark:text-[#f0f0f2]">Normalize Keys & Formatting:</strong> Keep "Sort Keys" toggled on to activate our recursive <strong>json key sorter</strong>. If your JSON has trailing commas or single quotes, click "Smart Fix" to repair them automatically with our built-in <strong>json validator</strong>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-[#111111] dark:text-[#f0f0f2]">Review the Semantic Diff:</strong> Switch between "Side-by-Side" and "Unified" view modes. Red highlights denote removed properties, green highlights denote added keys, and amber highlights indicate modified values.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-[#111111] dark:text-[#f0f0f2]">Export Findings:</strong> Click "Copy Patch" to extract the RFC 6902 <strong>json patch</strong> delta, or copy the formatted JSON directly into your project repository.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

